            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"IT (renamed via Postman)\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/departments/{{seeded_department_id}}", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["departments", "{{seeded_department_id}}"] },
            "description": "#28 — seeded_department_id defaults to the real seeded IT department. Safe, reversible rename."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "10. Delete Department (seeded — expect 409)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/departments/{{seeded_department_id}}", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["departments", "{{seeded_department_id}}"] },
            "description": "#29 — the seeded IT department has live members (mark, fah), so this genuinely 409s DEPARTMENT_HAS_DEPENDENTS. Real, not a bug."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "11. Delete Project",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/projects/{{created_project_id}}", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["projects", "{{created_project_id}}"] },
            "description": "#21 — 204, assuming \"6. Delete Source\" already ran."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Payments & Reimbursement Approval",
      "description": "POST /payments (#37), POST /payments/approve (#40), POST /reimbursements (#41, plumbing), POST /reimbursements/:id/status (#47), GET /reimbursements/:id/document (#48), POST /reimbursements/import (#49). Uses real seeded data: project TCOS Annual Event 2026, department Finance, source Booth Sponsor A — deliberately NOT the project created in folder 3, since that one has no real StaffDept rows for anyone (see docs/backend/04-authorization.md §1: admin/global role does not bypass project-scoped isFinance/isHead checks).\n\nRun order (approval chain): 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 (Finance login) → 5 → 6 (Owner login) → 6b (re-verify as beam) → 7 → 7b. Payments: 8 → 9 (Finance login + step-up) → 10 → 11. Import: 12 (needs a manually-attached CSV, see its description).\n\nA reauth token (X-Reauth-Token) is scoped to whoever verified it — re-run Verify Password for the new actor right before the step that needs it (5, 6b, 9 all do this).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "0. Setup notes (read me)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/health", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["health"] },
            "description": "Three real actors, three real roles — chompoo (head+finance of Finance dept), golf (finance of the project), beam (owner). All share the seed password Passw0rd!2026. service_token is SERVICE_TOKEN_ENROLL from api/.env."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "1. Login (chompoo — head+finance)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "if (pm.response.code === 200) pm.collectionVariables.set('chompoo_token', pm.response.json().data.access_token);"
          ] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"chompoo@tcos.app\",\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rd!2026\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Create Reimbursement (auto-verify)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
            "  pm.collectionVariables.set('reimbursement_id', pm.response.json().data._id);",
            "  pm.test('auto-verified straight to head_approve (chompoo heads this department)', () => {",
            "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.latest_status).to.eql('head_approve');",
            "  });",
            "}"
          ] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{chompoo_token}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"department_id\": \"{{department_id}}\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Postman verification run\",\n  \"details\": [\n    { \"title\": \"\\u0e04\\u0e48\\u0e32\\u0e2d\\u0e38\\u0e1b\\u0e01\\u0e23\\u0e13\\u0e4c\", \"amount\": 12000 }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/reimbursements", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["reimbursements"] },
            "description": "#41 — chompoo is head of {{department_id}}, so this lands straight in head_approve. meta.budget is a real computed projection."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Document — request, html (ใบเบิกเงิน)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{chompoo_token}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/reimbursements/{{reimbursement_id}}/document?type=request&format=html",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["reimbursements", "{{reimbursement_id}}", "document"],
              "query": [{ "key": "type", "value": "request" }, { "key": "format", "value": "html" }]
            },
            "description": "#48 — real rendered HTML. type=voucher would 422 NOT_APPROVED right now — not yet at fin_approve."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Login (golf — finance)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "if (pm.response.code === 200) pm.collectionVariables.set('golf_token', pm.response.json().data.access_token);"
          ] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"golf@tcos.app\",\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rd!2026\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Status: head_approve -> fin_approve",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
            "  const rt = pm.response.json().data.reauth_token;",
            "  if (rt) pm.collectionVariables.set('reauth_token', rt);",
            "}"
          ] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{golf_token}}" },
              { "key": "X-Reauth-Token", "value": "{{reauth_token}}" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"fin_approve\",\n  \"tracking_id\": \"{{tracking_id}}-{{$timestamp}}\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/reimbursements/{{reimbursement_id}}/status", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["reimbursements", "{{reimbursement_id}}", "status"] },
            "description": "#47 — needs a real X-Reauth-Token; if this 401s REAUTH_REQUIRED on a cold Runner pass, it's because folder 1's Auth reauth_token belonged to a different actor — run \"9. Verify Password (as golf)\" isn't reached yet this early, so within THIS folder the very first status change relies on the access_token's own recent verify; if it fails, run Verify Password as golf manually once. tracking_id is timestamp-suffixed for safe re-runs. golf is real finance on this project (StaffDept query, not mock scope)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Login (beam — owner)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "if (pm.response.code === 200) pm.collectionVariables.set('beam_token', pm.response.json().data.access_token);"
          ] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"beam@tcos.app\",\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rd!2026\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "6b. Verify Password (get step-up token, as beam)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "if (pm.response.code === 200) pm.collectionVariables.set('reauth_token', pm.response.json().data.reauth_token);"
          ] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{beam_token}}" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rd!2026\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/verify-password", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["auth", "verify-password"] },
            "description": "A reauth token is scoped to whichever staff_id verified it. Step 5's token belongs to golf; step 7's caller is beam, so it needs its own. Run this right before step 7 every time."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "7. Status: fin_approve -> transfer (rolls up totals)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{beam_token}}" },
              { "key": "X-Reauth-Token", "value": "{{reauth_token}}" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"transfer\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/reimbursements/{{reimbursement_id}}/status", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["reimbursements", "{{reimbursement_id}}", "status"] },
            "description": "#47 — owner-only (real role check). Rolls the ฿120.00 total up to department.total_expense/project.total_expense for real (no trigger does this). Needs the reauth token from \"6b\" — step 5's token belongs to golf and will 401 REAUTH_REQUIRED here even though still valid, wrong person."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "7b. Document — voucher, html (now valid)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{golf_token}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/reimbursements/{{reimbursement_id}}/document?type=voucher&format=html",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["reimbursements", "{{reimbursement_id}}", "document"],
              "query": [{ "key": "type", "value": "voucher" }, { "key": "format", "value": "html" }]
            },
            "description": "#48 — ใบสำคัญจ่าย. 422'd NOT_APPROVED before step 7; now latest_status is transfer, so it renders. golf sees the full bank account number (is_finance)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "8. Ingest Payment (service token, #37)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const body = pm.response.json();",
            "if (body && body.data) pm.collectionVariables.set('payment_id', body.data._id);"
          ] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Service-Token", "value": "{{service_token}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"_id\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n  \"source_id\": \"{{source_id}}\",\n  \"expected_amount\": 20000,\n  \"promptpay_qr_data\": \"00020101021229370016A000000677010111...\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/payments", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["payments"] },
            "description": "#37 — no Bearer token, X-Service-Token instead. {{$guid}} gives a fresh UUID each run, so this collection is safely re-runnable."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "9. Verify Password (get step-up token, as golf)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "if (pm.response.code === 200) pm.collectionVariables.set('reauth_token', pm.response.json().data.reauth_token);"
          ] } }],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{golf_token}}" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rd!2026\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/verify-password", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["auth", "verify-password"] },
            "description": "5-minute reauth token, scoped to golf. Overwrites reauth_token for both the payment-approve requests below."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "10. Approve Payment (bulk, #40)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{golf_token}}" },
              { "key": "X-Reauth-Token", "value": "{{reauth_token}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"decisions\": [\n    { \"payment_id\": \"{{payment_id}}\", \"status\": \"approved\", \"actual_amount\": 20000 }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/payments/approve", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["payments", "approve"] },
            "description": "#40 — golf is real finance on this payment's project. Rolls source.actual_amount (and project/tag total_income) up for real."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "11. Reject a payment (single-item batch)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{golf_token}}" },
              { "key": "X-Reauth-Token", "value": "{{reauth_token}}" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"decisions\": [\n    { \"payment_id\": \"{{payment_id}}\", \"status\": \"rejected\" }\n  ]\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/payments/approve", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["payments", "approve"] },
            "description": "#40 — there's no separate single-approve endpoint; a batch of one is how you approve/reject just one. Reports \"skipped\" since payment_id was already decided in step 10."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "12. Bulk Import Reimbursements (CSV, #49)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{golf_token}}" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                { "key": "project_id", "value": "{{project_id}}", "type": "text" },
                { "key": "file", "type": "file", "src": [] }
              ]
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/reimbursements/import", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["reimbursements", "import"] },
            "description": "#49 — needs a real CSV attached to the `file` field manually (Postman can't embed one in collection JSON); will 400 \"file required\" on an unattended run otherwise. Columns: requester_email,department,purpose,title,amount[,tag]. See `api/tests/fixtures/reimbursement-import.csv`."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
